{title: Terror on Every Side}
{subtitle: 1 Chronicles 24:14; Ezra 2:37; Nehemiah 7:40; Ezra 10:20; Jeremiah 20:1–3; 1 Chronicles 9:12}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 77}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] [F/A] | [Gm7] [Bbmaj7/F] | [Eb] | [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]David sorted the [F/A]priests in order
The [Gm]sixteenth line was [Eb]given to Immer
[Bb]In the temple they [F/A]kept the watch
[Gm]Serving the God of the [Eb]house
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Pashhur son of the [F/A]priest
Heard the [Gm7]prophet speak the [Eb]words
[Bb]Beaten and bound in the [F]stocks
At the Upper Ben[Eb]jamin Gate
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Exile ended and they [F/A]came home
[Gm7]A thousand and fif-[Eb]ty-two returned
[Bb]The sons of Immer walked [F/A]back
To the [Gm7]city of the [Eb]Lord
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]Morning light broke the si[F/A]lence
[Bb]Jeremiah spoke [Eb]his truth
[Gm]The name meant terror he [F/A]said
On [Eb]every single side
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The [Gm]line endured through the [F]years
[Eb]Faithful to the temple ground
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm7] | [Eb] |
